# The hook suite imports this library, and CPython caches compiled modules
# beside the source. Those artefacts are interpreter- and architecture-specific
# and stale the moment the .py changes, so they never belong in git.
#
# scripts/test-agent-hooks.py also sets sys.dont_write_bytecode and exports
# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, which stops them being created at all. This file
# is the second line of defence, for anyone who imports the library another way.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
